WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.684
The implementation track teaches the
same estate from the engineer's chair,

2
00:00:04.684 --> 00:00:09.538
in build modules from DNS and address
management through to day-two operations.

3
00:00:09.538 --> 00:00:11.812
The order is a real dependency chain.

4
00:00:11.812 --> 00:00:16.357
You address before you identify,
identify before you shape transport,

5
00:00:16.357 --> 00:00:21.137
and so on, and day two comes last because
it runs what everything else built.

6
00:00:21.137 --> 00:00:24.550
Every module ends the same
way: done means it works and

7
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:27.962
its evidence has landed where
an assessor can read it.

8
00:00:27.962 --> 00:00:30.362
And every lab teaches three habits.

9
00:00:30.362 --> 00:00:32.200
Observe before you enforce.

10
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.463
Keep a way back in, with emergency
access accounts created first.

11
00:00:36.463 --> 00:00:39.125
And export the record, not a screenshot.

12
00:00:39.125 --> 00:00:42.975
Certifications are examples,
not proof, and they change.

13
00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:47.173
One major Microsoft security exam
was just retired and replaced,

14
00:00:47.173 --> 00:00:51.137
so the program re-checks its
certification list at every gate.

15
00:00:51.137 --> 00:00:53.350
So how does the program certify people?
